WEBVTT

00:00:07.333 --> 00:00:10.633
Welcome to the wonderful world of animals.

00:00:11.866 --> 00:00:14.566
Find out what it is like to be an animal!

00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:21.800
Their world looks, sounds and smells different!

00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:26.266
Can you smell the air with your tongue?

00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:30.100
Or look for food with your face?

00:00:31.833 --> 00:00:37.099
Or see in the dark? Animals really are amazing.

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:41.433
They are real 'super- animals'.

00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:48.466
Do you know which is one of the strongest animals? Almost.

00:00:49.133 --> 00:00:51.866
It's a rhinoceros, but not this kind.

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:55.333
It's a rhinoceros beetle!

00:00:56.900 --> 00:01:02.800
This beetle can lift something that is 100 times heavier than its own body weight.

00:01:03.766 --> 00:01:05.399
Try lifting a car!

00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:10.666
Snow leopards have very strong legs.

00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:18.000
They can jump farther than any other animal, more than 15 metres.

00:01:19.300 --> 00:01:21.633
That's longer than a school bus.

00:01:23.966 --> 00:01:26.199
Some animals are really fast.

00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:30.466
The cheetah is the fastest land animal.

00:01:32.166 --> 00:01:35.866
It can run up to 98 kilometres per hour!

00:01:37.100 --> 00:01:44.500
That's as fast as a car! Other animals don't hurry ever.

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:47.800
Like this three-toed sloth.

00:01:49.100 --> 00:01:51.500
It's the slowest animal on earth!

00:01:53.266 --> 00:01:56.832
It sleeps most of the day and doesn't move very much.

00:01:58.800 --> 00:02:02.466
In the wild, it can live up to 16 years.

00:02:04.166 --> 00:02:07.466
But can you guess which animal lives the longest?

00:02:08.866 --> 00:02:14.366
It's the deep-sea sponge! Yes, sponges are animals, too.

00:02:16.033 --> 00:02:18.433
Some are thousands of years old.

00:02:20.366 --> 00:02:26.266
They can live longer than the Greenland shark, one of the world's largest carnivores.

00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:30.400
It <i>only</i> lives 400 years.

00:02:32.066 --> 00:02:39.732
Some animals are very clever: the lyrebird from Australia can copy any sound it hears.

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:43.900
It's better than a recording. Listen.

00:02:47.633 --> 00:02:48.966
Do you know the sound?

00:02:50.066 --> 00:02:51.966
Pretty amazing, don't you think?